<%# 3.1 "How it works" — illustrated vertical steps (design booklet page 29) %>
<div class="homepage-how-it-works" id="learn-more">
  <div class="row">
    <div class="hiw-content__headings">
      <h2><%= _("How it works") %></h2>
      <p class="hiw__subtitle">
        <%= _("You have the <strong>right</strong> to request information " \
              "from any publicly-funded body, and get answers. " \
              "{{site_name}} helps you make a Freedom of Information " \
              "request. It also publishes all requests online.",
              :site_name => site_name) %>
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="hiw-steps">
      <li class="hiw-step">
        <div class="hiw-step__illustration" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined">edit_document</span>
        </div>
        <div class="hiw-step__content">
          <h3 class="hiw-step__title"><span class="hiw-step__num">1.</span> <%= _("Make a request") %></h3>
          <p><%= _("Easily create a request by filling in your case. We have helped you by creating a template where you only need to state which documents you want access to. The request is sent to the chosen authority as an email, which they must respond to within a few weeks.") %></p>
          <%= link_to _("Make a request"), select_authority_path, class: "link_button_green" %>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="hiw-step hiw-step--reverse">
        <div class="hiw-step__illustration" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined">mark_email_unread</span>
        </div>
        <div class="hiw-step__content">
          <h3 class="hiw-step__title"><span class="hiw-step__num">2.</span> <%= _("Wait for a response") %></h3>
          <p><%= _("While the authority works on providing the documents you requested, you can sit back &mdash; we will notify you by email when you get a response. In the meantime, you can read other requests our users have made.").html_safe %></p>
          <%= link_to _("Browse requests"), request_list_successful_path, class: "button-secondary" %>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="hiw-step">
        <div class="hiw-step__illustration" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined">public</span>
        </div>
        <div class="hiw-step__content">
          <h3 class="hiw-step__title"><span class="hiw-step__num">3.</span> <%= _("Published and done") %></h3>
          <p><%= _("The answer is published online for everyone. Now you have your answer, and everybody else can access it too &mdash; contributing to public benefit and your right to know.").html_safe %></p>
          <%= link_to _("Search requests"), request_list_successful_path, class: "button-secondary" %>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</div>

<%# Dark "learn more about how we work" band with the accent notch %>
<div class="homepage-learn-more ds-dark">
  <div class="row">
    <h2 class="learn-more__title"><%= _("Learn more about how we work") %></h2>
    <p class="learn-more__text">
      <%= _("Public records need to be easier to access, to contribute to the common good and give society value &mdash; for our right as citizens to know what happens with our tax money. Dive into how our entirely non-profit organisation works and handles the process of helping you make so-called requests for public records.").html_safe %>
    </p>
    <div class="learn-more__ctas">
      <%= link_to _("Learn more about us"), help_about_path, class: "link_button_green" %>
      <%= link_to _("Support our work"), help_credits_path(:anchor => 'helpus'), class: "button-secondary" %>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
